    "camoufox": {
      "$comment": "OPTIONAL: the Camoufox browser binary, staged on demand by dep_ensure('browser'). An install that never browses never downloads ~650MB. Without this pin camoufox-js picks the browser at INSTALL TIME: its postinstall queries the GitHub releases API and regex-matches the newest asset in a '>=alpha.1, <1' range, so two machines installing on different days get different browsers and an unauthenticated caller can be rate-limited (60 req/hour) into no browser at all. Hermes points camoufox-js at this staged copy with CAMOUFOX_INSTALL_DIR, so it never calls that API. win32-arm64 maps to the x86_64 zip on purpose: upstream ships no ARM build for Windows (camoufox-js's own OS_ARCH_MATRIX is win: x86_64/i686), so ARM runs it emulated -- UNVERIFIED on real hardware, and the alternative is no browser at all.",
      "version": "152.0.4-beta.28",
      "optional": true,
      "files": {
